THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
--------------------

Nothing is downloaded from a third party at run time.

This action downloads and executes exactly one archive, ours, verified against a
digest pinned in pins.env before anything in it runs. It fetches nothing else,
from anyone.

That archive BUNDLES Trivy, and the scanner EXECUTES it. This differs from the
other Visiblaze actions, which only adapt rules from it:

Trivy - https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy
    Copyright Aqua Security Software Ltd.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

    The release archive contains the Trivy binary and its Rego policy bundle.
    `visiblaze-iac` invokes Trivy to evaluate infrastructure files and then
    normalises its report. Trivy is shipped inside our archive rather than
    fetched separately so that one digest covers everything that executes, and
    so that a scan never depends on a registry being reachable.

    Trivy's output is NOT forwarded. Its report carries the offending source
    lines verbatim; the normalisation step reads them on your runner to derive
    the resource address and discards them. See SECURITY.md.

    A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is in LICENSE, which is the same
    licence Trivy is distributed under.
